WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.690
Hi friends!

00:00:00.690 --> 00:00:04.702
Today we're going to explore a big, special number: one hundred!

00:00:04.702 --> 00:00:07.711
We use one hundred all the time, at school, with

00:00:07.711 --> 00:00:09.215
money, and when we play.

00:00:09.215 --> 00:00:11.221
Let's find out why it's so cool!

00:00:11.921 --> 00:00:13.450
Count with me by tens!

00:00:13.450 --> 00:00:18.937
Ten, twenty, thirty, forty, fifty, sixty, seventy, eighty, ninety, one hundred!

00:00:18.937 --> 00:00:19.215
See?

00:00:19.215 --> 00:00:21.646
Ten groups of ten make one hundred.

00:00:21.646 --> 00:00:23.313
That's how we get there!

00:00:23.913 --> 00:00:24.799
Look at money!

00:00:24.799 --> 00:00:26.948
One hundred cents make one dollar.

00:00:26.948 --> 00:00:30.489
If you save one hundred pennies, or four shiny quarters,

00:00:30.489 --> 00:00:32.006
you have a whole dollar.

00:00:32.006 --> 00:00:32.639
Cha-ching!

00:00:33.239 --> 00:00:36.039
Have you heard people say one hundred percent?

00:00:36.039 --> 00:00:38.657
One hundred percent means all of something.

00:00:38.657 --> 00:00:41.762
If you eat one hundred percent of your cookies, you

00:00:41.762 --> 00:00:43.041
ate every single one.

00:00:43.041 --> 00:00:43.649
None left!

00:00:44.249 --> 00:00:45.453
Here's a hot fact!

00:00:45.453 --> 00:00:48.327
Water boils at one hundred degrees Celsius.

00:00:48.327 --> 00:00:52.204
When a kettle hits one hundred, steam comes whooshing out.

00:00:52.204 --> 00:00:53.006
Don't touch!

00:00:53.006 --> 00:00:55.279
Ask a grown-up to show you safely.

00:00:55.879 --> 00:00:58.654
Words with centi are about one hundred.

00:00:58.654 --> 00:01:02.496
A centimetre is one hundredth of a metre — super tiny!

00:01:02.496 --> 00:01:04.987
And a century is one hundred years.

00:01:04.987 --> 00:01:07.121
Wow, that's a long, long time.

00:01:07.721 --> 00:01:09.929
Imagine living one hundred years.

00:01:09.929 --> 00:01:12.337
That's a century-old birthday party!

00:01:12.337 --> 00:01:15.816
People blow out one hundred candles on a giant cake.

00:01:15.816 --> 00:01:17.087
What a celebration!

00:01:17.687 --> 00:01:20.978
Draw a square with ten little boxes across and ten

00:01:20.978 --> 00:01:22.163
little boxes down.

00:01:22.163 --> 00:01:24.927
Fill them in and count: one, two, three...

00:01:24.927 --> 00:01:27.691
all the way to one hundred little squares!

00:01:27.691 --> 00:01:28.481
Neat, right?

00:01:29.081 --> 00:01:32.233
People say a centipede has one hundred legs.

00:01:32.233 --> 00:01:33.523
But that's a myth!

00:01:33.523 --> 00:01:37.105
Centipedes can have lots and lots of legs, but not

00:01:37.105 --> 00:01:39.039
always exactly one hundred.

00:01:39.039 --> 00:01:39.684
Surprise!

00:01:40.284 --> 00:01:44.513
So remember: ten tens, one hundred cents, one hundred percent,

00:01:44.513 --> 00:01:47.788
boiling water, centuries, and a ten-by-ten grid.

00:01:47.788 --> 00:01:49.766
You can count to one hundred.

00:01:49.766 --> 00:01:51.676
Great job, number explorers!
